<section class="source-doc-transcript">
  <h2 id="returning-to-the-fold">Returning to the Fold</h2>

  <p>I was helping Forest Cadwell with a group of hunters in the mid 1960s for a break from mining silver ore. We were in elk country and one of the gentlemen was having some problems walking, at times he appeared to be in considerable pain. His companions kidded him about his ailment, one of them asked him if he had passed any stitches that day and laughed.</p>

  <p>We were resting and eating lunch on an open hillside. Cal was sitting to the left of Forest and said, "I might as well tell you fellows about my accident before my friends get the story all out of proportion. My wife and I live in the country and we have some livestock as well as chickens, just about what the two of us can handle...Dora woke me one night, back in September, and said the chickens were raising a fuss so I put my pants on over my pajamas, grabbed a flashlight and my .22 caliber pistol and went out to check on them. When I got to the coop I stuck the pistol in my pants by the buckle so I could open the door...I shined the light around and a skunk was just going out the far end...I started to pull the pistol out and the darned think discharged...shot me right in the penis."</p>

  <p>"How many times did it go off, Cal?"</p>

  <p>"It just went off once."</p>

  <p>"How many wounds did you get, Cal?" the same man asked.</p>

  <p>"I had two entry wounds and two exit wounds in my penis and one hole in my left thigh where the bullet lodged. I know what Tom's getting at, but it wasn't all that extraordinary, when I put my pants on over my pajamas it sort of...you know...folded things up a little."</p>

  <p class="source-doc-note"><em>Cal and Dora are given no surname and are not otherwise identified on this site.</em></p>
</section>

<section class="source-doc-transcript">
  <h2 id="please-moo-before-you-drop-in">Please Moo Before You Drop In</h2>

  <p>Ranchers are slow to adapt to urban conveniences. They aren't stubborn, it's just that when you are brought up in an environment where a little baling wire, a pair of pliers and a daub of grease will keep the wheels turning they aren't anxious to get involved in anything like plumbing or propane stoves.</p>

  <p>Bathrooms, however, did come to the Cebolla Creek area due to the urging of housewives and tourists. Owners of a ranch at the junction of Spring and Cebolla Creeks had a bathroom installed for the caretakers. This was the era of cesspools and grease traps before we learned that septic tanks were safer and less polluting than a rocked up hole in the ground with a wooden deck over it.</p>

  <p>John Martin was enjoying his morning constitutional on one of the new-fangled china stools with a week old newspaper in his hands when one of his cows grazed upstream and crossed their backyard headed for green shoots by a fence. Her route took her directly over the cesspool and a dirt covered platform that hadn't been designed for a cow-path.</p>

  <p>A thousand pounds of potential beef patties disappeared in one grand "whoosh" accompanied by an equal amount of dirt and broken boards. The sudden overloading of the cesspool caused a reverse flush that nearly lifted John from the john.</p>

  <p>There he sat, his outdated evening edition well splattered and water dripping from unmentionables, wondering if the Russians had just dropped a bomb on us or Earth's rotation had suddenly changed directions.</p>

