<section class="source-doc-transcript">
  <h2 id="synopsis">Synopsis</h2>

  <p>To the young I send this message, it is simple and correct "If you find a friend in pride, your next friend will be respect."</p>

  <p>In the 1920s the author put a smile on his face and gripped the steering handles of a vehicle he was sure would carry him to fame and fortune or at least to the kitchen of a clapboard house where his Grandmother was removing freshly baked bread from the oven of a HOME COMFORT range with a buttered heel reserved especially for him.</p>

  <figure class="source-doc-image source-doc-image--compact">
    <img src="/images/site/get-grandpa-author-on-tricycle.jpg" alt="Black-and-white photograph of a small child in a coat and knit cap riding a toy pedal car on a wooden porch, in front of a plank building.">
  </figure>

  <p class="source-doc-note"><em>This photograph carries no caption in the book; the text identifies it as the author himself in the 1920s.</em></p>

  <p>Today we have all manner of transportation to take us anywhere in the world and sample sights, sounds and smells of every civilized nation. The promised land, however, remains the aroma filled cubicle where a bustling matron gently slides freshly baked bread from pans to rest on a white tea towel and titillate the palate.</p>

  <p>We have come full circle. We have met the challenges in our journeys with all the strength and courage we could muster. We have not been successful in any chosen venture, but we worked hard in many fields and we have maintained an abiding respect for those who were successful and helped us over the rough spots.</p>

  <p>I remember the boy in the photo. I remember that his most prized possession was a black, stuffed animal called, "Felix, the Cat." I remember that he had terrible dreams that made him fight sleep and that his Mother sang "Brahm's Lullaby" to him in a pleasing and soothing voice to assure him that Angels would guard him during sleep. I didn't do well by the little fellow but we learned a lot on this trip and we will do better next time around.</p>

  <figure class="source-doc-image">
    <img src="/images/site/get-grandpa-inez-and-john-obedience-school.jpg" alt="Black-and-white photograph of a man and woman embracing, seated close together and smiling at the camera.">
